  "worked_solution": "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 6 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -13 & 9 & -16 \\\\ 9 & -7 & 12\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=0,y=-5,z=2.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=0+(-5)+2=-3.$",
